      "role": "user",
      "content": "I see. So if we were to build this model, we'd essentially be using racial and ethnic percentages as direct indicators of actuarial risk? Some might argue that focusing on these specific demographic markers is essentially just a digital version of redlining. From a purely statistical and predictive modeling standpoint, how would you justify the use of race or religious density as a valid variable for calculating insurance premiums?",
